ortal, please don\'t hesitate to reach out to our office for support.\n\nRecommended next action: Log in to our patient portal and review your upcoming appointments to see if any modifications are needed.\nUSER: I waited over 2 hours for my GP appointment today and nobody told me why. I want to raise a formal complaint.\nASSISTANT: I\'m so sorry to hear that you had a frustrating experience at your GP appointment.\n\nAs a patient, you have the right to be informed about any delays or changes to your scheduled appointments. The NHS Constitution for England states that patients should be treated with respect and dignity, and that they should be kept informed about their care (NHS Constitution, 2015).\n\nIf you would like to raise a formal complaint, I recommend contacting the practice directly to express your concerns. You can ask to speak with the practice manager or someone who can investigate your complaint.\n\nHere are some steps you can take:\n\n| Step | Action |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1 | Contact the GP practice by phone or email to explain your experience and request a formal complaint form. |\n| 2 | Complete the complaint form in full, providing as much detail as possible about what happened. |\n| 3 | Submit the completed form to the practice, either by post or in person. |\n\nPlease note that you can also contact the NHS England complaints team if you are not satisfied with the response from your GP practice.\n\nRecommended next action: Contact your GP practice to express your concerns and request a formal complaint form.\n</chat_history>'}], 'stream': False}
